; Under --group-by-cumulative a register keeps the postings' running total
; from group to group but not the accounts' display state.  P2's only
; posting to A is virtual, so its row prints as (A), exactly as it does
; without --group-by-cumulative; account A still carries
; ACCOUNT_EXT_HAS_NON_VIRTUALS from group P1 if the accounts' xdata
; survives the flush, and the row then prints as A.  The first block
; passes on the unfixed tree and pins the output that clearing only the
; postings' xdata would break.

2012/01/01 P1
    A                                       $10
    B

2012/01/02 P2
    (A)                                      $5

test reg --group-by payee --group-by-cumulative -s --depth 1 A
P1
12-Jan-01 - 12-Jan-01           A                               $10          $10

P2
12-Jan-02 - 12-Jan-02           (A)                              $5          $15
end test

test reg --group-by payee --group-by-cumulative -s --dow --depth 1 A
P1
12-Jan-01 - 12-Jan-01           A                               $10          $10

P2
12-Jan-02 - 12-Jan-02           (A)                              $5          $15
end test
